        "listicle3section2_U74VKf": {
          "type": "listicle3section2",
          "name": "Blog split layout34",
          "settings": {
            "image_max_width": 450,
            "image_border_color": "#224b38",
            "heading": "<p>1. Your hairbrush looks worse every<br/>single day</p>",
            "paragraph_1": "<p>Most people assume it’s just genetics. It usually isn’t the whole story.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p>When product residue and excess oil build up along the scalp, they form a barrier that clogs follicles and starves them of nutrients. Hair can’t grow the way it’s supposed to — so it thins. <strong>And falls.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Reniva’s Thuja Orientalis and Ginger Extract at full botanical strength </strong>break down that buildup layer. Jojoba Oil gets natural moisture flowing again so follicles aren’t starved in the first place.</p>",
            "background_color": "#224b38",
            "text_color": "#ffffff",
            "vertical_padding": 30,
            "heading_size": 24,
            "text_size": 16,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "listicle3section3_WGRWer": {
          "type": "listicle3section3",
          "name": "Blog split layout343",
          "settings": {
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_vertical": 5,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "<p>2. Your scalp gets itchy for no clear<br/>reason</p>",
            "heading_size": 28,
            "paragraph_1": "<p>An irritated scalp tends to flare up more at night, when natural oil production shifts and a full day of product buildup has had time to settle in.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p>Most people chalk it up to dandruff or dry skin. <strong>It’s rarely just that.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Thuja Orientalis</strong> has been used for generations specifically for this. It calms scalp irritation at the source, not just the surface itch.</p>",
            "paragraph_size": 16,
            "text_gap": 0,
            "paragraph_gap": 0,
            "text_color": "#000000",
            "image_width": 70
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "listicle3section2_6D8peW": {
          "type": "listicle3section2",
          "name": "Blog split layout34",
          "settings": {
            "image_max_width": 450,
            "image_border_color": "#224b38",
            "heading": "<p>3. Your part looks wider than it<br/>used to</p>",
            "paragraph_1": "<p>This one surprises people the most.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p>Thinning at the part and crown often gets written off as “just how your hair falls.” It’s usually early follicle fatigue — <strong>something in your routine isn’t giving those roots what they need.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Hydrolyzed Oat Protein and Ginseng Extract</strong> rebuild strength from the root up, while the rest of the formula supports the follicle directly. Most people notice less fall by week two.</p>",
            "background_color": "#224b38",
            "text_color": "#ffffff",
            "vertical_padding": 30,
            "heading_size": 24,
            "text_size": 16,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "listicle3section3_di4kxJ": {
          "type": "listicle3section3",
          "name": "Blog split layout343",
          "settings": {
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_vertical": 5,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "<p>4. Your hair won’t grow past a certain length no matter what you try</p>",
            "heading_size": 28,
            "paragraph_1": "<p>Breakage isn’t always about split ends. When strands are dry and brittle at the root, they snap long before they ever reach the length you’re after.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p><strong>You’re not failing at growing your hair out. Your strands are working against you.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Hydrolyzed Oat Protein</strong> in Reniva’s formula reinforces the hair shaft from within, reducing the breakage that’s been capping your length.</p>",
            "paragraph_size": 16,
            "text_gap": 0,
            "paragraph_gap": 0,
            "text_color": "#000000",
            "image_width": 70
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "listicle3section2_yxcn8y": {
          "type": "listicle3section2",
          "name": "Blog split layout34",
          "settings": {
            "image_max_width": 450,
            "image_border_color": "#224b38",
            "heading": "<p>5. You avoid certain hairstyles because of thinning spots</p>",
            "paragraph_1": "<p>When thinning becomes visible at the part or crown, most people start adjusting — a different part, more volumizing product, avoiding ponytails.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p>Most people try more product or a different cut. <strong>They never address the scalp underneath.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Five botanicals working together</strong> at the source, not masking the symptom. When the scalp finally gets what it needs, the thinning slows down — and regrowth has a chance to catch up.</p>",
            "background_color": "#224b38",
